{"id": "EUVD-2026-86177", "enisaUuid": "313368e6-2129-3dd0-995f-4d87f929d28f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mvm: fix out-of-bounds tid_data access in BA notif\n\nmvmsta->tid_data was indexed by the TFD loop counter 'i' instead of\nthe actual TID value 'tid'. This writes lq_color into a random tid_data\nslot unrelated to the BA entry.\nSince multi-TID blockack is not really in use, 'i' was always 0 and no\nharm was done.\nAdd a out-of-bound check before accessing the array.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:57:25", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35f991d685feafd27255bd33272512c434e52527", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c48b741277b01b2c3b4ecccedc72fc575b71dc04", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8ac5e91b1296f65c3d119fac3fa917ff458f811", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94d3982806c7f194b23484befde12934dda23064"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rh32-7cxx-qxq4", "CVE-2026-93790"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "519a386d-f8e9-34d1-8b3b-095aeb26eb1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "7cf71201-f79b-350e-9df2-c3e85253976a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "8c9e9088-ee16-3d45-9cf2-702f56f4a489", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41fd2fec56db2564f02532ed7244e1f69193b4ad <35f991d685feafd27255bd33272512c434e52527"}, {"id": "a2e42121-7358-3787-84a1-fcaf64511201", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "a865d10c-200f-3f2f-af6a-0cef5ea3be46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cf022d48-d57f-3d3d-a4a9-d605c01977a3", "pr